  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated shelter and camp coordination and camp management support for displacement-affected communities in Cabo DelgadoIntegrated shelter and camp coordination and camp management support for displacement-affected communities in Cabo Delgado</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to provide coordinated assistance to displaced individuals in Cabo Delgado, Mozambique focusing on two primary intervention components: Shelter and Non-food Items (NFI) and Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM). The intervention targets four vulnerable districts including Chiure, Ancuabe, Muidumbe, and Macomia. The response addresses urgent shelter needs and provides NFIs, while also ensuring effective coordination and management of displacement sites through CCCM activities, with the objective of ensuring the safety and dignity of affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
